DTEND:20260729T000000Z
DTSTAMP:20260728T000000Z
SUMMARY:What Makes Magic… Magic?
DESCRIPTION:What Makes Magic… Magic? is an original  theatrical 
 presentation by Bill Wisch that explores the art and psychology behind 
 astonishment. Far more than a traditional magic show\, this unique 
 experience defines\, explains\, and demonstrates the five key psychological 
 elements that make magic so captivating to watch.\n\nDesigned primarily for 
 adult audiences\, the program has also proven highly successful for ages 
 eight and older. It features exceptional sleight-of-hand magic combined 
 with fascinating behind-the-scenes insights into the world of professional 
 magic and performance. A highlight of the presentation is its rare 
 perspective on the legacy of Tony Slydini\, widely regarded as one of the 
 two most influential sleight-of-hand artists of the twentieth century. As 
 Slydini’s protégé beginning in 1976\, Bill Wisch shares stories\, 
 principles\, and performance philosophies drawn from this remarkable 
 relationship.\n\nCombining mystery\, entertainment\, history\, and 
 psychology\, What Makes Magic… Magic? offers audiences a deeper 
 appreciation of the artistry and timeless appeal of magic while showcasing 
 the extraordinary talents and insights of Bill Wisch\, a professional 
 magician with more than fifty-five years of experience.
LOCATION:Nutley - Children's Room
ORGANIZER;CN="Nutley Library":MAILTO:events@nutley.bccls.org
CATEGORIES:
UID:LibCal-10315-16306275
URL:https://bccls.libcal.com/event/16306275
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTART:20260729T140000Z
DTEND:20260729T150000Z
