SUMMARY:RUST - Film Screening and Discussion with Marylou & Jerome Bongiorno
DESCRIPTION:RUST:  Film Screening and Discussion\nSaturday\, August 1\, at 
 2:00 p.m.\n\nDiscussion will follow the film screening with award-winning 
 filmmakers Marylou & Jerome Bongiorno and Special Guest\, Edwin 
 Ortiz\n\nRUST (Documentary\, 2021\, 86 min.) RUST is the third documentary 
 in Marylou & Jerome Bongiorno’s 3Rs Trilogy on Urban America\, following 
 the success of critically acclaimed\, award-winning\, national PBS 
 broadcast REVOLUTION ’67 (2007) on riots/rebellions of the 1960s and THE 
 RULE (2014) on urban school reform. RUST presents the history of Rust Belt 
 poverty\, detailing industrialization and deindustrialization\, racism and 
 mass incarceration\, using the city of Newark\, New Jersey as a microcosm. 
 It explores solutions to inner city poverty through the voices of 
 scholars\, economists\, physicians\, activists\, and the community.  The 
 filmmakers will lead then a lively discussion addressing questions about 
 the filmmaking process and their process in documenting social justice 
 issues.\n\nNo registration is required. Light refreshment will be served. 
 Screening will be held on the 2nd Floor of the Library and will begin at 
 2:00 p.m.\n\nTo learn more about Bongiorno Productions visit: 
 bongiornoproductions.com.\n\nTo view the trailer visit: 
 https://vimeo.com/502830434.\n\nEdwin Ortiz founded the “Returning 
 Citizens Support Group” in Newark\, which "provides critical reentry 
 support services for systems-impacted communities of color.” To learn 
 more visit: returningcitizensnj.org.\n\nThis program is made possible in 
 part by funds from the New Jersey State Council on the Arts /  Department 
 of State\, a Partner Agency of the National Endowment for the Arts and 
 administered by the Essex County Division of Cultural and Historic Affairs.
LOCATION:Nutley - Children's Room\, Nutley Free Public Library
ORGANIZER;CN="Nutley Library":MAILTO:events@nutley.bccls.org
CATEGORIES:
UID:LibCal-10315-17149608
URL:https://bccls.libcal.com/event/17149608
END:VEVENT
