SUMMARY:Library Speakers Consortium - High Altitudes and High Stakes: A Miss Marple Mystery with Lucy Foley
DESCRIPTION:You must register here to attend: 
 https://libraryc.org/nutleypubliclibrary/187080\n\nJoin us for a thrilling 
 conversation with acclaimed author Lucy Foley as we delve into her 
 brand-new Miss Marple mystery\, Murder at the Grand Alpine Hotel. \n\nHigh 
 in the Swiss Alps\, accessible only by a single\, winding railway\, stands 
 the luxurious Grand Alpine Hotel. With glorious mountain views and 
 exclusive access to powdery slopes\, it draws guests from far and wide. 
 \n\nThe notorious actress. \n\nThe high-flying politician. \n\nThe society 
 wife. \n\nThe reckless friend. \n\nThe shrewd doctor. \n\nBut not everyone 
 is here for a winter holiday. Beneath the champagne and furs\, dark 
 histories simmer\; old grudges emerge like cracks in the ice. And someone 
 is watching from the shadows. A polite\, unassuming woman with an 
 extraordinary mind: Miss Marple. When a body is found and a blizzard cuts 
 off all escape\, only Miss Marple can connect the clues before the killer 
 strikes again. Because it isn’t a question of who has a motive\, but 
 who’s next…\n\nAbout the Author:\n\nLucy Foley is a No.1 Sunday Times\, 
 Irish Times and New York Times bestselling author. More than 10 million 
 copies of her books are in print worldwide\, and several are currently 
 being adapted for the screen. She is a Waterstones Thriller of the Month 
 author\, a three-time nominee at the British Book Awards\, and The Guest 
 List was a Reese’s Book Club selection and winner of the Goodreads Choice 
 Award for Mystery Thriller. As a life-long Agatha Christie fan\, Lucy has 
 drawn immeasurable inspiration from the Queen of Crime. She was one of 12 
 writers to contribute to Marple\, a collection of short stories featuring 
 the beloved detective. And in Murder at the Grand Alpine Hotel\, she was 
 inspired to transport Miss Marple – her favorite Christie creation – to 
 the glamorous post-war setting of the Swiss Alps\, in a mystery that feels 
 gloriously escapist yet utterly relevant to our times.
LOCATION:Nutley Free Public Library
ORGANIZER;CN="Nutley Library":MAILTO:events@nutley.bccls.org
CATEGORIES:Author Event/Talk
UID:LibCal-10315-17136356
URL:https://bccls.libcal.com/event/17136356
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTART:20260827T220000Z
DTEND:20260828T000000Z
DTSTAMP:20260827T000000Z
SUMMARY:Tarot 201: The Fool's Journey
DESCRIPTION:Thursday\, August 27\, 2026 from 6:00 PM to 8:00 PM.\n\nNo 
 registration required! \n\nAre you ready for a leap of faith?!\n\nThis 
 event is for anyone who has previously attended Tarot 101 with Kate and/or 
 gained basic tarot skills independently. If you’re familiar with the 
 Major and Minor Arcana and you know how to shuffle and pull the cards\, 
 then you’re ready for 201!\n\nDuring our time together\, Kate will 
 explore in more depth the esoteric and spiritual principles behind the 
 tarot\, particularly the Major Arcana as seen through the lens of Jungian 
 psychology. Taking us along the Fool’s Journey\, Kate will offer card 
 interpretations that continue to move beyond making predictions and instead 
 focus on conscious evolution and soul growth.\n\nAttendees are encouraged 
 to bring a notebook and pen\, plus your favorite tarot deck (if you have 
 one). The program will begin with an extended Q&A troubleshooting session\, 
 particularly for those who have attended Tarot 101\, so feel free to come 
 prepared with questions!\n\nWhile this program is designed with relative 
 beginners in mind\, more intermediate tarot learners may benefit from this 
 in-depth review of foundational concepts.\n\nAbout the presenter: Kate 
 Sheridan\, a.k.a. The Laundress\, is a tarot reader and astrologer who 
 believes that each one of us can make our own magic. Her approach is 
 healing rather than predictive\, and her work is deeply informed by Jungian 
 psychology. You can find her on Instagram @themodernlaundress or online at 
 thelaundresstarot.com.
LOCATION:Nutley - Stockton Room\, Nutley Free Public Library
ORGANIZER;CN="Nutley Library":MAILTO:events@nutley.bccls.org
CATEGORIES:
UID:LibCal-10315-17219682
URL:https://bccls.libcal.com/event/17219682
END:VEVENT
