BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTART:20260912T180000Z
DTEND:20260912T200000Z
DTSTAMP:20260912T000000Z
SUMMARY:Blanket Making Meetup - to benefit Project Linus
DESCRIPTION:All adults 18  are welcome to join us for some socializing and 
 stitching!  We are making blankets for babies and children ages 0-18. 
 Donations are coordinated via Project Linus\, an organization that works 
 with hospitals\, shelters and agencies in North Jersey.  Please read the 
 guidelines below carefully.\n\nBlankets can be knit or crochet. 
 Coffee/tea/cookies will be served.\n\nThe Guidelines:\n\n\n	Please bring 
 your own project/materials!\n	Finished blankets must be new\, unused\, and 
 of excellent quality.\n	Yarn must be acrylic\, cotton or cotton/poly blend 
 (no wool) and washable.\n	Materials must be clean\, free from smoke and pet 
 hair and other contaminants. Hospitals in particular are unable to accept 
 blankets that are in less than pristine condition.\n	Do not launder yarn\, 
 as detergents may have scents or chemicals that can’t be used around the 
 recipients.\n	Blankets will be given to children of all ages\, from infant 
 to teen\, so ideal sizes would be from about 36x36 inches (newborn) and 
 up.\n	Can’t join us on the 12th? Finished blankets may be dropped off to 
 the reference desk till the end of the day on Friday\, September 25.\n\n\n 
 \n\nQuestions?  Please call the library at 973-667-0405 ext. 2604 or email 
 marisa.treglio@nutley.bccls.org
LOCATION:Nutley - Stockton Room\, Nutley Free Public Library
ORGANIZER;CN="Nutley Library":MAILTO:events@nutley.bccls.org
CATEGORIES:Special Event
UID:LibCal-10315-17344047
URL:https://bccls.libcal.com/event/17344047
END:VEVENT
